1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,064
Claude Code is great, but today it has
three problems.

2
00:00:04,414 --> 00:00:05,075
One.

3
00:00:05,425 --> 00:00:07,879
It does one task at a time, and you wait.

4
00:00:08,229 --> 00:00:08,975
Two.

5
00:00:09,325 --> 00:00:14,147
You cannot see what each helper agent
does, or how the work was split between
them.

6
00:00:14,497 --> 00:00:15,286
Three.

7
00:00:15,636 --> 00:00:17,065
It stops when you stop.

8
00:00:17,415 --> 00:00:20,509
Nothing moves your project forward while
you are away.

9
00:00:22,009 --> 00:00:23,929
symcc solves all three.

10
00:00:24,279 --> 00:00:26,135
It is a plugin for Claude Code.

11
00:00:26,485 --> 00:00:29,002
You talk to one lead, in your normal chat.

12
00:00:29,352 --> 00:00:33,320
The lead keeps a shared task board, and
workers take the tasks from it.

13
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:36,377
First, no more waiting.

14
00:00:36,727 --> 00:00:41,154
Workers run tasks side by side, each in
its own copy of your code,

15
00:00:41,154 --> 00:00:43,703
so they never get in each other's way.

16
00:00:44,053 --> 00:00:46,763
Your tests must pass before anything is
merged.

17
00:00:47,113 --> 00:00:51,017
And when one task needs another, the lead
puts them in the right order.

18
00:00:52,517 --> 00:00:54,458
Second, you can see everything.

19
00:00:54,808 --> 00:00:58,268
Every task on the board shows what it is,
why it exists,

20
00:00:58,268 --> 00:01:01,357
which files it may change, and where it
came from.

21
00:01:01,707 --> 00:01:06,571
You also see its tries, the worker's
report, and the time and tokens it cost.

22
00:01:06,921 --> 00:01:09,718
Review each change and approve it
yourself,

23
00:01:09,718 --> 00:01:13,556
or choose auto mode, and passing work is
merged right away.

24
00:01:13,906 --> 00:01:16,615
If a worker has a question, it waits for
you.

25
00:01:18,115 --> 00:01:20,419
Third, it keeps going while you are away.

26
00:01:20,769 --> 00:01:25,015
Scouts wake up on timers and look for
bugs, missing tests, and gaps.

27
00:01:25,365 --> 00:01:29,119
The lead turns what they find into tasks,
and workers do them.

28
00:01:29,469 --> 00:01:31,773
You come back to finished, tested work.

29
00:01:33,273 --> 00:01:37,881
symcc is free and open source, under the
MIT license.

30
00:01:38,231 --> 00:01:41,773
Install it as a plugin for Claude Code,
with one command.

31
00:01:42,123 --> 00:01:43,232
symcc.

32
00:01:43,582 --> 00:01:46,633
Many agents, one board, working while you
are away.
